{{External|rs=Quests/Strategy}}{{See also|Optimal quest guide/Ironman|Optimal quest guide/Free-to-play}} 
The '''optimal quest guide''' lists ''[[Old School RuneScape]]'' [[quests]] in an order that allows new [[Members]] to progress in a way that minimises the amount of [[skill]] training to completion of all the quests. This guide does '''not''' show the most efficient quest order. It does not take into consideration [[unlockable content]], such as [[fairy rings]] or [[dragon equipment]], that provide numerous benefits to the player's game progression. For that, it is recommended that players complete the quests in the [[Optimal quest guide#Notable_quest_unlocks|notable quest unlocks]] section as soon as possible.

==Guide==
[[Experience lamp]]s or [[book of knowledge|books of knowledge]] received through [[random events]] or [[Achievement Diary|Achievement Diaries]] may be used on any skill of the player's choosing or to save time by shortening the next bit of training in this guide.

Players with 50 [[Construction]] should take advantage of their [[player-owned house]] for access to a [[portal chamber]], [[teak altar]], and [[amulet of glory (mounted)|mounted glory]]. [[Teleport to House|Teleport to house]] ([[Teleport to house (tablet)|tablet]]) may also be used for emergency teleport. New players on a budget should use a [[ring of dueling]] to access the bank and restore stats at [[Ferox Enclave]]'s [[pool of refreshment]].

Completing [[Achievement Diary|Achievement Diaries]] will be beneficial throughout the game; some of the [[Achievement Diary Rewards|rewards]] include access to [[Ardougne cloak 1|unlimited teleports]], noted item drops, [[antique lamp]]s, [[shortcuts]], and additional [[Lunar_spellbook|lunar spells]]. Similarly, some [[miniquests]] may provide useful rewards, such as experience lamps, and may be required to complete other quests.

{{Optimal quest guide/Recommended Quests}}

===Quests===
A note on usage ('''particularly relevant for new players'''): the "New levels after quest" column shows the levels the player will have if they follow this guide exactly. However, players may find it beneficial to train up [[Agility]] (for faster run regeneration and eventually the [[graceful outfit]]) and one's combat stats (especially [[Prayer]] for [[protection prayers]]) separately to make completing some quests easier. This is not strictly necessary, though, as [[stamina potion]]s and [[energy potion]]s can also be used to restore run energy, and many quest bosses can be [[Flinching|flinched]] or [[safespot]]ted, thereby circumventing the need for strong stats and gear. 

Hover over a skill reward in the "New levels after quest" column to see the exact total experience in the listed skill after completing the quest.
